{\pard\sa200\sb300\b\fs34 Master Project Context \u8212? Advanced Video Editor\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Consolidated:** 2026-11-16 | **Repository:** https://github.com/anneshabiswaas22-collab/advance-video-edior\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Status:** Ongoing commercial software development, NOT a mock UI/prototype and NOT yet commercially production-ready.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Source of truth:** Latest main branch + CI + Issues + ADRs. This document summarizes current available project conversation and inspected repository; dates/links below are snapshots.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 1. Founder's mission and outcome\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 Create an original, independently branded, extensible, high-quality video editing platform for:\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - YouTubers and everyday creators who value simplicity and quick edits;\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - professional editors and filmmakers needing precision, color, sound, masking, compositing and production workflow;\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - content teams needing automation, social delivery, reusable templates and Windows support.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Product benchmarks, not source to copy:** CapCut (ease of use, templates, effects, AI), Adobe Premiere Pro (precision/nonlinear editing and professional workflows), DaVinci Resolve (color/audio/compositing and post-production). Do not claim equivalent feature completeness or copy proprietary code, designs or assets.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Primary targets:** Web browser and native Windows desktop. Future systems/platforms can be considered if they do not derail the main goal. Cross-platform architecture is a design consideration, not verified deployment support.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 **Development values:** working code > glossy demos, validated exports > containers/screenshots, one coherent editor > wholesale combinations, reuse-first > unnecessary new implementations, trustworthy attribution/license compliance > unlicensed downloads, free/local when possible > recurring inference bills.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 2. Operating constraints and instructions\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Use the strongest available reasoning for real architecture and code. User permits deep investigation (up to ~2 hours if an execution environment supports it), but do not artificially spend that time; reserve substantial effort for implementation.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Minimize credit and cost. No paid AI APIs, premium inference, external uploads of original footage, paid media generation or unlicensed checkpoints/assets without explicit approval.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Prefer locally run/open-source utilities, mock AI providers in CI, deterministic short media fixtures, existing Vitest and Playwright setup, FFmpeg/ffprobe validation, and caching in CI.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Inspect latest main and all relevant docs before implementation. Read AGENTS.md, docs/CODEX_REVIEW_QUEUE.md, docs/CODEX_HANDOFF.md, related ADRs/evidence, and the 22-reference inventory.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Current OpenReel import is provisional but real. Keep its project schema, timeline authority, editing commands and export pipeline unless objective tests justify a full migration.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Do not merge incompatible timeline models, render pipelines, project storage schemes, history engines, or full alternative editor repositories.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Reuse existing code and dependencies first; add small typed adapters second; write fresh code only after demonstrating a gap.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Small focused tested changes; follow repository permissions; don't force-push or overwrite unrelated work. Earlier project AGENTS explicitly allowed non-destructive direct main commits, but reviewable PRs are appropriate for high-risk changes.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - No fake implementations presented as working, no unsubstantiated Windows/4K/GPU claims, no blanket license clearance.\par}
