{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 5. Canonical architecture principles\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **One project format:** IDs, media library, track and clip ownership, title/caption timeline, serialization.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **One editing command contract:** state validation, undo/redo, timeline notifications, project scoping; no AI direct mutation of filesystem or uncontrolled network calls.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **One export truth:** preview and rendered export must use validated shared timing/composition semantics. Different acceleration backends may exist behind an adapter, but must produce consistent tested content.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Stable source media linkage:** source handles, blobs, source-file metadata, relinking, save/reopen and package import/export must be tested across sessions.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Local-first privacy:** user files should not upload unless requested with informed opt-in.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Windows constraints:** enforce safe native filesystem boundaries; document FFmpeg binary origin/config and installers/signing.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Performance:** use WebCodecs/MediaBunny/native FFmpeg capabilities already present, test proxy and worker paths, memory/buffer lifecycle, handling of unsupported codecs and GPU fallback.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Licensing:** code MIT at upstream root is not blanket clearance; audit dependencies, codec binaries, model weights, templates, fonts, music, stock media and assets separately.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - **Reproducibility:** pinned Node/pnpm toolchain; deterministic media; same fixtures/hardware for comparative benchmarking.\par}
\par
