{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 Most important correction to previous prompts\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 The original build prompt and ADR-0001 required "exactly two" leading editors, OpenReel and FreeCut. Follow-up discussion requested that **OpenCut also receive independent serious architectural evaluation**. The reconciled policy is:\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - One canonical editor engine / timeline / project schema: **provisionally OpenReel in editor/**.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - Up to two primary independent references: **FreeCut** and **current OpenCut rewrite**.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - OpenCut Classic is an **additional legacy study source**, not a fourth engine.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 - This is a research policy extension, not approval to merge 3 engines or migration evidence. ADR-0001 is historical; complete Issue #8 benchmarks before a final foundation choice.\par}
\par
