{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 Proposed equal-hardware benchmark protocol (Issue #8)\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 1. Record exact commit SHA, dependency snapshot, browser version, OS/CPU/GPU/RAM, sandbox conditions.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 2. Use identical deterministic 640x360 test media (red->blue cut, tone and independent WAV); then a realistic 1080p 30fps short fixture.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 3. Execute import/scrub/split/trim/title/audio/save/reopen/MP4 export using each editor's supported workflow.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 4. Collect measured import, seek, render latency, peak memory, crash/failure and file size.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 5. Decode every export; assert expected cut pixels, title visibility, PCM tone windows and relative alignment.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 6. Distinguish native Windows/GPU/4K from Chromium/Linux and unsupported cases; mark NOT TESTED.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 7. Review code/asset/model/transitive licenses, maintainer recent activity, issue backlog and adapter surface.\par}
{\pard\sa80\fs20 8. Log measurements in docs/evidence and update ADR-0001 or create a successor ADR with explicit migration/rollback criteria.\par}
\par
{\pard\sa180\sb300\b\fs28 Known high-priority failure modes to detect\par}
\par
{\pard\sa80\fs20 Off-by-one cut; title visible in UI but absent from MP4; wrong media source after recovery; silent/missing audio; wrong audio start/tail, failed waveform or channel mix; fallback encoder produces different composition; memory leaks during long export; unavailable browser codec; relink references lost on reopen; destructive agent/tool call; unlicensed model/FFmpeg redistribution.\par}
